2026-09-27T04:47:38.1717508Z Description:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1717995Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1718448Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1719659Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1721041Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1721170Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1721465Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1721887Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1722298Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1722447Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1722753Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1722929Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1723148Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1723702Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1724038Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1724214Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1724624Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1724876Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1725117Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1725730Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1726445Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1727520Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1728469Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1728651Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1729308Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1730217Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1730708Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1731209Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1731934Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1732085Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1732378Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1732551Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1734717Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1737259Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1737634Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1738438Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1739236Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1740251Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1741242Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1823871Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1824534Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1825251Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1825718Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1826172Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1827934Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1830005Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1831044Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1832396Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1832724Z 
